reminders: rolling 7-day window instead of fixed T-1

Every tick now reminds about every assignment due in 0..window_days (default
7), so a task due next week is mentioned tonight and every evening until it
is due. Deadlines that already passed are treated as done and never
mentioned again, which also keeps historical lectures quiet.

- reminders.window_days (default 7); 0 falls back to the exact days_before
  offsets, so the old behaviour stays available.
- Candidates are ordered by urgency (fewest days left first).
- One message per assignment per day; the dedupe key already encodes the
  remaining days, so tomorrow's reminder is a new key.
- remind --dry-run prints the window and the shortlist.
